    "body": "> As noted on Matrix we need to account for service workers and in particular \"handle fetch\". Either we make it so that \"handle fetch\" returns a controller for the service worker fetch event, or we pass the controller into \"handle fetch\" so the service worker can observe it. The former seems a bit nicer as it reuses the pattern introduced here and could be used for other kinds of information exchange in the future. It would require \"handle fetch\" to take a callback.\r\n> \r\n> @yutakahirano @jakearchibald @noamr thoughts?\r\n\r\nI like the idea of returning a controller from SW's fetch rather than having SW query its caller fetch for \"is terminated\"... \r\nDoes it affect this PR?",
